// `#[valid]` finds the nested function **by name** -- `<snake>_violations` of the field's own type
// -- which is the rule F243 settled for every generator dependency: a function written by hand will
// do, and a type from another module needs its `_violations` imported, exactly as
// `#[derive(Json)]` needs its `_to_json`.
//
// **Reported generically, by the call that does not resolve.** `src/derive.c` checked this by
// reading `#[valid]` off each field and looking the name up, which bought "add derive(Validate) to
// 'Plain'" at the price of the compiler knowing what a field attribute means. That was the last
// such name and it went on 2026-10-30; what is left names the file, the declaration, the generator
// and the missing function, and is the same report any generator gets for any unresolved call. The
// better message returns when a generator can declare the names its output needs
// (docs/design/user-generators.md §5b).
struct Plain {
    city: string
}

#[derive(Validate)]
struct E {
    #[valid]
    home: Plain
}

fn main() {
    print(1)
}
